---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContentPage from '../../components/ContentPage.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About Us"
  description="Learn why SummaryIn exists, how its resume summary tools work, and how examples are researched and reviewed."
  yearInTitle={false}
>
  <ContentPage
    eyebrow="About SummaryIn"
    title="A practical starting point for a stronger resume"
    lead="SummaryIn helps people turn real work experience into a short, specific resume summary without an account, a paywall, or a blank page."
  >
    <h2>Why we built SummaryIn</h2>
    <p>
      Writing three useful lines about yourself is surprisingly difficult. Most advice says to be
      confident, concise, and specific, but it rarely shows what that looks like for a nurse, driver,
      teacher, warehouse worker, or someone applying for a first job.
    </p>
    <p>
      SummaryIn was built to close that gap. Each profession guide combines a simple generator with
      examples for different experience levels, stronger verbs, and clear prompts for adding proof.
      The goal is not to write a perfect resume for you. It is to give you a credible first draft that
      is easy to edit and genuinely sounds like your work.
    </p>

    <h2>How the generator works</h2>
    <p>
      The free generator uses templates stored in the page itself. Your role, skills, experience level,
      and tone are combined in your browser to create several options. The text you enter is not sent
      to an AI service or saved in a SummaryIn database.
    </p>

    <h2>How we approach examples</h2>
    <p>We write profession pages around the details employers can evaluate:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the setting, specialty, customer, or type of work;</li>
      <li>the tools, systems, certifications, or equipment used;</li>
      <li>the size and pace of the workload;</li>
      <li>a result that can be explained in an interview.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Numbers shown in square brackets are prompts, not claims. They are there to remind you to replace
      the sample metric with something true from your own experience. We avoid invented employers,
      fake testimonials, and promises that a particular summary will guarantee an interview.
    </p>

    <h2>Free first, useful first</h2>
    <p>
      The core generator and examples are free to use. SummaryIn may later link to resume builders or
      other career services. If a link is sponsored or earns a commission, it will be identified. A
      commercial relationship will not determine which examples or writing advice appear on the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and feedback</h2>
    <p>
      Job language changes, and no example fits every workplace. If you spot an unclear claim, outdated
      term, or missing profession, send it through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Useful
      corrections are welcome.
    </p>
  </ContentPage>
</Base>
